  "result": "I found the bug and wrote the fix plan to `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\the-help-output-looks-piped-quokka.md`. Plan mode is on, so I haven't edited any code, and the tool for submitting the plan for approval isn't available in this session.\n\n**Cause:** `join_options()` in `src/click/formatting.py:319` sorts each option's names with `reverse=True`. That puts long names first, so `--help` shows `--help, -h` and `--verbose, -v` instead of the usual `-h, --help` and `-v, --verbose`. The test at `tests/test_commands.py:188` already expects `-h, --help`. I also checked the code that decides the order of the options themselves (the decorators, `get_params`, `format_options` and `write_dl`), and it's correct.\n\n**Fix:** a one-line change that removes `reverse=True`:\n```python\nrv.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n```\nNames with the same prefix length stay in the order they were declared.\n\n**Verification:** run `pytest tests/test_commands.py tests/test_formatting.py tests/test_options.py -q`, then the full suite. Then check by hand that `--help` shows `-v, --verbose` and `-h, --help`.\n\nIf you approve, I'll make the change and run the tests.",
